      },
      "message": "test: follow the LinuxCNC preamble (#4196) and Tormach G54.1 P offsets (#4299)\n\nTwo posts changed on purpose and three suites on main still read the old\noutput:\n\n- #4196 writes G92.1 G97 in the LinuxCNC preamble. The mirror trace model\n  refused both codes (\"G92.1 is not modelled\"), and the flipped-x golden\n  had the old line. G92.1 clears G92 offsets (the trace models none) and\n  G97 sets rpm mode; neither moves the tool. The golden diff is exactly\n  that preamble line.\n- #4299 raised Tormach's offsets to 500 (G54.1 P10-P500). wcs_index and\n  the UI combo test still expected nine. The setup command keeps its own\n  bound (MAX_SLOT + 1 = 255), so the combo lists 255 entries.\n\nNo product code changes.\n\nFixes #4322\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
